From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pessi-v <pessimo@posteo.net>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:28:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] (hybris) init: do not mount a tmpfs over /apex

apexd is not run on this adaptation. The APEX payloads that are needed
(runtime linker and libraries) are provided in /apex by the Sailfish OS
side before droid-hal-init starts. The stock tmpfs mount would hide them
behind an empty directory that nothing fills.
---
 init/init.cpp |   10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/init/init.cpp b/init/init.cpp
index 2b32a4db33f93a835b123abf287a32a062119670..6b351aee25bda61f53db8229bc6475b5a0499b7f 100644
--- a/init/init.cpp
+++ b/init/init.cpp
@@ -649,9 +649,13 @@ static void MountExtraFilesystems() {
 #define CHECKCALL(x) \
     if ((x) != 0) PLOG(FATAL) << #x " failed.";
 
-    // /apex is used to mount APEXes
-    CHECKCALL(mount("tmpfs", "/apex", "tmpfs", MS_NOEXEC | MS_NOSUID | MS_NODEV,
-                    "mode=0755,uid=0,gid=0"));
+    // lilac: apex is never activated on this Sailfish-hosted setup. Leaving /apex
+    // as-is (a plain persistent directory on this rootfs, pre-populated with real
+    // linker binaries -- see /apex/com.android.runtime/bin) instead of shadowing it
+    // with a fresh noexec tmpfs apexd would otherwise populate but never runs here.
+    // was:
+    // CHECKCALL(mount("tmpfs", "/apex", "tmpfs", MS_NOEXEC | MS_NOSUID | MS_NODEV,
+    //                 "mode=0755,uid=0,gid=0"));
 
     // /linkerconfig is used to keep generated linker configuration
     CHECKCALL(mount("tmpfs", "/linkerconfig", "tmpfs", MS_NOEXEC | MS_NOSUID | MS_NODEV,
